	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "EI19Y_Z3p_jhM0eU2",
			"description": "Auramite Power Armour (Aquilon Pattern)",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 3: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 3 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it. Gap DR: arm 53, leg 53.\n\nUnlike an Astartes power armour Mark, Aquilon pattern leaves no significantly weaker location: every hit location carries substantial DR, per the framework's explicit instruction. Requires no black-carapace-style interface - a Custodian's own physiology and training suffice - and imposes no fine-motor or DX penalty even on a wearer without one, since it is built individually for its wearer from the start.\n\nLore: Aquilon pattern Auramite armour is the standard plate of the Legio Custodes across current Codex: Adeptus Custodes background and Chris Wraight's Custodes novels: golden, ornate, and consistently described as superior in every respect to Astartes power armour, matched to the wearer's own body rather than issued from a common pool.\n\nDesign: Torso DR is the framework's own fixed Custodes anchor (150), 50 above Astartes power armour's Mk VII baseline (100). Limb/head DR use the same proportional offsets as the Mk VII Astartes family (Imperium/Armour/Imperial Armour.eqp), scaled by 150/100 = 1.5x: arm/ leg 88x1.5=132, neck 63x1.5=94.5 rounded to 95, skull 100x1.5=150, face 75x1.5=112.5 rounded to 113, hand 63x1.5=94.5 rounded to 95, foot 75x1.5=112.5 rounded to 113. Eye lenses are set to 112, three-quarters of the helmet's 150 (framework.md eye-lens rule, 112.5 rounded down), well above the Astartes Mk VII lens (75) because the helmet is half again as tough. Servo bonus (lifting_st +10, striking_st +6) is set a clear step above the Astartes Mark VII suite's own +9/+5, reflecting superior Custodes-grade actuators on top of the wearer's already much higher ST 40. Checked against the assignment's calibration requirement: a standard boltgun (6dx2(2) pi++, eff. DR vs torso = 150/2 = 75) penetrates Auramite only 0.0% of the time by exact dice distribution (6d is at most 36, so 6dx2 never exceeds 72, always below 75) - a Custodian in Auramite shrugs off bolter fire completely, stronger even than the assignment's baseline expectation of \"should shrug off bolter fire,\" and a marked step up from an Astartes' own 14% chance of being hit through his own plate.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
