						}
					],
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "eLyRaMdnTleRQiE2s",
					"description": "Auramite Energy Field (Integrated)",
					"local_notes": "Shield 120 SP. Recharge: after 3 seconds without taking damage, regains 20 SP per second (twice the delay after it collapses). Blocks ranged and melee attacks, all locations. Tracked with the Uses counter as for any field (framework.md \"Personal force fields\").\n\nLore: Custodes plate carries its own energy field, the source of the Custodians' invulnerable protection on the tabletop (a 4+ save, the same as an Iron Halo) and of the fiction's shots and blows that flare off a Custodian before they reach the gold.\n\nDesign: The Iron Halo's numbers (Imperium/Armour/Fields.eqp): the same 4+ invulnerable save in the lore, so the same pool, delay and recharge. It holds a plasma bolt (avg 84) and a krak grenade's average (84) and recovers in seconds; a lascannon still breaks it.",
					"tags": [
						"Force Field",
						"Energy Shield"
					],
					"base_value": "20000",
					"base_weight": "0 lb",
					"uses": 120,
					"max_uses": 120,
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "EHKI13_agc8MmYrtV",
			"description": "Allarus Terminator Armour",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 3: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 3 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it. Gap DR: arm 88, leg 88.\n\nEffective SM +1 while worn on top of a Custodian's own unarmoured SM +1 (total SM +2), the bulkiest infantry-portable armour in the setting. Requires no black-carapace-style interface, as Auramite above. Life support allows unaided teleportation and extended void operations, as Astartes Terminator plate.\n\nLore: Allarus Custodians - the Legio Custodes' Terminator-analogue elite - wear this pattern per current Codex: Adeptus Custodes background, consistently described as heavier and more protective than an Astartes Terminator's own Tactical Dreadnought Armour, matching the framework's fixed Allarus anchor.\n\nDesign: Torso DR is the framework's own fixed anchor (250), 50 above the Astartes Tactical Dreadnought (Terminator) anchor of 200. Limb/head DR scale by 250/200 = 1.25x from the Indomitus-pattern Terminator armour's own values (Imperium/Armour/Imperial Armour.eqp): arm/leg 175x1.25=218.75 rounded to 220, neck 138x1.25=172.5 - deliberately pulled down slightly to 158 rather than following the multiplier exactly, since a straight 1.25x on every location would leave the neck disproportionately strong relative to the arm/leg figures; skull 200x1.25=250, face 150x1.25=187.5 rounded to 188, hand 125x1.25=156.25 rounded to 158, foot 150x1.25=187.5 rounded to 188. Eye lenses set to 188, three-quarters of the helmet's 250 (framework.md eye-lens rule, 187.5 rounded up), a clear step above the Astartes Terminator's 150 and this file's own Auramite lens (112), matching Allarus plate's status as the single best infantry armour modelled in this project. Servo bonus (lifting_st +22, striking_st +12) sits above the Astartes Indomitus Terminator suite's own +20/+10. An extra +1 SM (stacking to SM +2 total with the wearer's own unarmoured SM +1) reflects Allarus plate's even greater bulk than Auramite armour, mirroring how the Astartes Terminator suit adds SM +1 over that wearer's own SM 0 baseline; -1 Basic Move follows the same convention. Checked against the assignment's calibration requirement (a standard boltgun, eff. DR vs torso = 250/2 = 125): penetration is 0.0% by exact dice distribution, comfortably beneath even Auramite's own already-total immunity to bolter fire.",
