					"description": "Allarus Energy Field (Integrated)",
					"local_notes": "Shield 120 SP. Recharge: after 3 seconds without taking damage, regains 20 SP per second (twice the delay after it collapses). Blocks ranged and melee attacks, all locations. Tracked with the Uses counter as for any field (framework.md \"Personal force fields\").\n\nLore: Allarus plate carries its own energy field, the source of the Custodians' invulnerable protection on the tabletop (a 4+ save, the same as an Iron Halo) and of the fiction's shots and blows that flare off a Custodian before they reach the gold.\n\nDesign: The Iron Halo's numbers (Imperium/Armour/Fields.eqp): the same 4+ invulnerable save in the lore, so the same pool, delay and recharge. It holds a plasma bolt (avg 84) and a krak grenade's average (84) and recovers in seconds; a lascannon still breaks it.",
