		{
			"id": "EuwnHeOx4skOk6vE7",
			"description": "Vratine Armour",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 4: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 4 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nFull-enclosure ceramite plate over a padded underlayer; imposes the usual GURPS bulky-armour DX/Stealth penalties for rigid heavy armour, as any carapace-class suit. Built for an unaugmented human body, exactly as Adepta Sororitas power armour is: no black- carapace-style interface of any kind is needed or possible for a Sister of Silence.\n\nLore: Vratine armour is the Sisters of Silence's standard-issue plate per current Codex: Adeptus Custodes background (which covers the Sisterhood alongside the Legio Custodes) and The Master of Mankind's depiction of Sisters operating on Terra; framework.md classes it as carapace-tier rather than true power armour, matching its consistently more austere, masked-helm silhouette relative to Custodes gold.\n\nDesign: Torso DR held at the fixed Carapace anchor (70, framework.md), the same tier used for the Imperium's other elite carapace suits (Tempestus, Arbites patterns). Non-torso figures scale from the Arbites Pattern carapace suit's own full-head-enclosure, hands-and- feet-covered profile (Imperium/Armour/Imperial Armour.eqp: arm/leg 36, neck 41, skull 45, face 34, hand 23, foot 27) by the anchor's own move from 45 to 70 (x14/9), since Vratine armour's enclosed, masked helm is closer to that design brief than the open-faced Guard pattern's: arm/leg 56, neck 64, skull 70, face 53, hand 36, foot 42; eye 52 is three-quarters of the helmet (framework.md eye-lens rule), not scaled.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Imperium",
				"Sisters of Silence"
			],
